DEMO -- files written FOR this collection, not collected with it.Everything else on this disk was gathered from public archives.  These fewfiles were not: they were written so the programs here have something towork on, and so the recipes in DOC/HOWTO can be run exactly as printed.  sphere.pgm    a 48x24 greyscale image in plain (ASCII) PGM format.  gulls.gif     a real photograph, 320x200, GIF87a.  NOT ours -- it came                as test material with a GIF viewer posted in 1992, and it                is here because the 169 converters in CMDS/NETPBM had no                photograph to work on.  See SOURCES.txt.Plain PGM is readable text, which is the point -- open it and the formatexplains itself: the magic number P2, then width and height, then themaximum grey value, then one number per pixel.Try it:  pnmfile /dd/DEMO/sphere.pgm            what it is, and how big  pgmtopbm /dd/DEMO/sphere.pgm | pbmtoascii     see it on the screen  pnminvert /dd/DEMO/sphere.pgm | pgmtopbm | pbmtoasciiThe NETPBM programs read from a pipe and write to a pipe, so they chain.DOC/HOWTO has more, including the ones that need a real file rather than apipe because they seek backwards in their input.